WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.904 --> 00:00:06.139
I am Charlotte Staerck,

00:00:06.139 --> 00:00:08.908
cofounder and CEO 
of Handbag Clinic.

00:00:08.908 --> 00:00:10.543
Today we're going
to be looking at

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:12.645
mold removal on a handbag.

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:16.783
[brush scraping]

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:20.954
This bag was actually at
the back of a wardrobe,

00:00:20.954 --> 00:00:23.957
and a pipe burst 
behind the wardrobe,

00:00:23.957 --> 00:00:26.226
which created 
the perfect area

00:00:26.226 --> 00:00:29.062
for mold to be spawned.

00:00:29.062 --> 00:00:33.933
[light scraping]

00:00:33.933 --> 00:00:35.735
Our artisan will
always start

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:37.771
by assessing the type
of mold that it is

00:00:37.771 --> 00:00:39.906
and making sure it's safe
for them to work on.

00:00:39.906 --> 00:00:42.575
From there, we will 
use a range of tools

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:46.212
to begin scraping the 
bulk of that mold off.

00:00:50.683 --> 00:00:52.085
They will select the tool

00:00:52.085 --> 00:00:55.255
that will be most successful
in removing that,

00:00:55.255 --> 00:00:57.657
but also avoiding any
scuffs or scratches

00:00:57.657 --> 00:00:59.259
to that leather underneath.

00:00:59.259 --> 00:01:03.730
[light scraping]

00:01:06.099 --> 00:01:08.101
In some areas we can
use a metal tool

00:01:08.101 --> 00:01:10.036
because the leather is a 
little bit harder wearing

00:01:10.036 --> 00:01:11.504
in those places

00:01:11.504 --> 00:01:14.741
and the mold is less
attached to the bag.

00:01:18.044 --> 00:01:20.680
We will go in with
the wooden tool

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:23.082
when we are getting a bit
closer to that leather,

00:01:23.082 --> 00:01:24.918
because we obviously 
don't want to scratch

00:01:24.918 --> 00:01:26.886
or damage that 
leather underneath.

00:01:28.855 --> 00:01:32.892
And we then go in with a 
brush to remove any excess

00:01:32.892 --> 00:01:34.928
that is dried on
the top as well.

00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:38.331
[brushing]

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:46.139
Once we have removed
as much dry mold

00:01:46.139 --> 00:01:47.407
as we possibly can,

00:01:47.407 --> 00:01:50.643
we then will start 
with the mold removal.

00:01:50.643 --> 00:01:52.645
This bag was so 
heavily saturated

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:55.114
we needed to make sure
we killed the mold

00:01:55.114 --> 00:01:57.584
that was going all the
way through that skin.

00:01:57.584 --> 00:02:00.120
A leather skin is 
absorbent in the same way

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:02.222
that our skin is absorbent,

00:02:02.222 --> 00:02:03.790
so we needed to make
sure we kill it

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:05.158
all the way through
to make sure

00:02:05.158 --> 00:02:07.660
that wouldn't come 
back at a later stage.

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:09.629
The artisan will spray

00:02:09.629 --> 00:02:12.966
the mold-removal solution
direct onto the bag.

00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:15.001
This is something that
we do not recommend

00:02:15.001 --> 00:02:16.369
that anybody tries at home.

00:02:16.369 --> 00:02:18.204
Any product going
on a leather

00:02:18.204 --> 00:02:19.973
should always go 
onto a cloth first,

00:02:19.973 --> 00:02:22.208
usually, because
spraying direct,

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:24.310
if you don't have the
correct training,

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:27.046
can lead to actually damaging
the leather further.

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:31.117
It's important that a bag 
that's saturated with mold

00:02:31.117 --> 00:02:33.086
is handled by professionals

00:02:33.086 --> 00:02:35.355
so that they are 
able to really kill

00:02:35.355 --> 00:02:36.823
the base of that mold

00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:38.258
to make sure it 
doesn't come back,

00:02:38.258 --> 00:02:41.661
spread to your other 
items in your wardrobe,

00:02:41.661 --> 00:02:43.663
and to make sure that
the bag's not damaged

00:02:43.663 --> 00:02:45.565
in the process as well.

00:02:51.204 --> 00:02:53.706
Once we've completed
the mold removal

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:56.543
and killed the actual
cause of the mold,

00:02:56.543 --> 00:02:59.078
we will then move on
to cleaning the bag

00:02:59.078 --> 00:03:01.247
to remove any 
additional chemicals

00:03:01.247 --> 00:03:03.216
and to hygienically
clean the bag,

00:03:03.216 --> 00:03:05.818
getting it ready to be 
returned to its client.

00:03:05.818 --> 00:03:07.754
The artisan is now applying

00:03:07.754 --> 00:03:09.756
our specialist 
in-house cleaner.

00:03:09.756 --> 00:03:12.458
This removes any 
additional chemicals

00:03:12.458 --> 00:03:14.027
that are left on the bag,

00:03:14.027 --> 00:03:16.262
making sure that we've
hygienically cleaned

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:18.398
the bag throughout as well.

00:03:18.398 --> 00:03:23.002
We are turning our leather
cleaner into a foam.

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:27.473
This just gives a very even 
coating throughout the item.

00:03:27.473 --> 00:03:30.243
It also creates a 
really nice lather

00:03:30.243 --> 00:03:33.446
to make sure it really 
gets into all of the skin

00:03:33.446 --> 00:03:35.715
and cleans it thoroughly.

00:03:35.715 --> 00:03:37.483
This bag has already
been through

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:39.218
so much cleaning
by this point.

00:03:39.218 --> 00:03:41.788
So we are simply
just wiping away

00:03:41.788 --> 00:03:43.790
any of those 
excess chemicals

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:46.159
and excess dirt on the bag.

00:03:49.028 --> 00:03:50.863
Once this process
is complete,

00:03:50.863 --> 00:03:54.334
this item is ready to 
go back to the client.

00:03:54.334 --> 00:03:58.605
This client had huge sentimental
attachment to this bag,

00:03:58.605 --> 00:04:01.241
really loved it, and didn't
think it was savable.

00:04:01.241 --> 00:04:03.376
And because we 
managed to save it,

00:04:03.376 --> 00:04:04.410
when they got it back,

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:05.912
they actually 
rang our office

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:08.181
and were crying with 
happiness down the phone

00:04:08.181 --> 00:04:09.515
that we'd saved their bag.

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:12.151
With the cleaning 
process, mold is tricky,

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:13.152
because you've 
got to make sure

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:16.289
you kill those enzymes that
are creating the mold.

00:04:16.289 --> 00:04:18.424
So they do need very
different products.

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:21.261
Even if a bag has a 
small amount of mold,

00:04:21.261 --> 00:04:24.530
it's important that you seek
help from a professional,

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:26.432
because you need to
kill the source.

00:04:26.432 --> 00:04:27.667
If you don't 
kill the source,

00:04:27.667 --> 00:04:29.936
it will just spread back
throughout that handbag.

00:04:29.936 --> 00:04:32.538
It also may spread to other
items in your wardrobe.

